{
  "analysis": "The VM starts but gets stuck immediately with no syscall or fwrite traces. The likely cause is the BSS zeroing: the .bss section is ~1GB (0x4003c6d0 bytes), and the `zeroRange` call is creating ~262K pages, which is extremely slow and memory-intensive. Since my sparse Memory class already returns 0 for uninitialized pages, I don't need to zero BSS at all. I should remove the zeroRange call for BSS.",
  "plan": "Remove the BSS zeroRange call in the ELF loader since sparse memory returns 0 for uninitialized pages. Also reduce syscall trace threshold and add early PC tracing to find where it gets stuck. Then re-test.",
  "commands": [
    {
      "keystrokes": "python3 - <<'PY'
src=open('/app/vm.js').read()
# Remove BSS zeroing - sparse memory returns 0 for uninitialized pages
src=src.replace('''    if (p_memsz > p_filesz) {
      mem.zeroRange(p_vaddr + p_filesz, p_memsz - p_filesz);
    }''', '''    // BSS is implicitly zero in sparse memory - no need to zero
    // if (p_memsz > p_filesz) mem.zeroRange(p_vaddr + p_filesz, p_memsz - p_filesz);''')
# Reduce syscall trace to first 100k and add early PC trace
src=src.replace("if (this.instCount < 1000000) console.error", "if (this.instCount < 100000) console.error")
# Add early PC tracing for first 100 instructions
trace = r'''    if (this.instCount < 100) console.error(`[trace] pc=${(pc>>>0).toString(16)} inst=${(inst>>>0).toString(16)} op=${(inst>>26)&0x3f} instCount=${this.instCount}`);
'''
src=src.replace("    const inst = this.mem.readU32(pc);\n    this.execute(inst, pc);", "    const inst = this.mem.readU32(pc);\n" + trace + "    this.execute(inst, pc);")
open('/app/vm.js','w').write(src)
PY
node -c /app/vm.js
",
      "duration": 0.1
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "rm -f /tmp/frame.bmp /tmp/vm_out.txt; timeout 10 node /app/vm.js > /tmp/vm_out.txt 2>&1; echo "exit=$?"; wc -l /tmp/vm_out.txt; head -80 /tmp/vm_out.txt; ls -la /tmp/frame.bmp 2>/dev/null
",
      "duration": 12.0
    }
  ]
}
